After the 3 real fixture webp files were copied onto the primary tree's
Admin/storage/app/public/conversation/ (making the 3 URLs distinct), a COLD app restart
+ single clean tap on any of message 91's 3 tiles reproduced ZERO Hero/framework errors
across 5 repeated open/close cycles (checked via `adb logcat -d --pid=<pid> | grep -i
FAIL/Exception/Error`, pid-scoped). So this specific collision is gated on the
missing-file/shared-placeholder condition, not on multi-attachment rendering itself; it
is a real latent fragility in the URL-keyed Hero tag (any 2+ attachments that resolve to
the same URL, e.g. duplicate uploads or a storage outage, will hit it), but it is not
reliably reachable via the ticket's normal happy-path demonstration once the fixture's
image files are actually servable.
